# Todo and Task Management Rules

## Code Organization
- Break down large features into smaller, manageable tasks
- Create TODO comments for future improvements
- Use consistent TODO format: `// TODO: [description]`
- Include context in TODOs: `// TODO: Add error handling for API failures`

## Task Prioritization
- High Priority: Critical bugs, security issues, blocking features
- Medium Priority: Performance improvements, UX enhancements
- Low Priority: Code refactoring, documentation updates

## TODO Comment Format
```javascript
// TODO: Add loading state for user profile
// TODO: Implement error boundary for this component
// TODO: Add unit tests for this function
// TODO: Optimize re-renders with useMemo
```

## Code Review Checklist
- [ ] All TODOs have clear descriptions
- [ ] No console.log in production code
- [ ] Components are properly typed (TypeScript or PropTypes)
- [ ] Error handling is implemented
- [ ] Loading states are handled
- [ ] Accessibility considerations (a11y)

## Feature Development
1. Plan the feature structure
2. Create component skeleton
3. Implement core functionality
4. Add error handling
5. Add loading states
6. Write tests
7. Document the component

## Best Practices
- Keep components focused on single responsibility
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks
- Use proper error boundaries
- Implement proper loading and error states
- Follow accessibility guidelines
